      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341778",
      ":question/problem": "Let $f(x)$ be the $2L$-periodic extension of a function $F(x)$ from $x\\in [-L,L)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({{field-1}})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({{field-2}}).\n$$\n\nThe $6$th sine coefficient of the series is\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $F(x)={x}^{3}$ and $L=3,$ the $6$th sine coefficient becomes\n\n$$\n{b}_{6}={{field-4}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-5}}.\n$$"
    },
